~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ Easy Rule to Remember

app/
  Pages & Routes

components/
  Reusable UI

hooks/
  Reusable Logic

services/
  API Calls

lib/
  Shared Libraries & Config

types/
  TypeScript Types

utils/
  Helper Functions


~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~For a Next.js + NestJS project, when you open a page file (app/users/page.tsx), you can mentally trace:

Page
 ↓
Hook
 ↓
Service
 ↓
Backend API
 ↓
Database

Then back:

Database
 ↓
Backend
 ↓
Service
 ↓
Hook
 ↓
Component
 ↓
Screen

That's the end-to-end request flow you'll see in most production applications.
